# /etc/hermes-watchdog.conf — operator config for hermes_watchdog.sh
# Root-owned, 0600. NOT in git: DEADMAN_URL is a per-install secret.
#
# DEADMAN_URL — health-gated dead-man's switch.
#
# The watchdog pings this URL ONLY on a run where the gateway is genuinely
# healthy. So "pings stopped" means one of: the gateway is unhealthy, the
# watchdog is dead, or the box is gone. All three are invisible to an on-box
# check, and the Telegram alert path is correlated with the very failure it
# reports (if Telegram or the network is down, the alert silently fails).
#
# NOTE: a naive dead-man's switch — a cron job pinging on a schedule — would
# NOT have caught either real outage. Cron delivery kept working for all four
# days of the Aug 21 incident. Health-gating is what makes this work.
#
# Setup (~2 min, free): create a check at https://healthchecks.io with period
# 5 min / grace 10 min, then paste its ping URL below and `systemctl restart
# hermes-watchdog.timer`. Any equivalent service works.
#
#DEADMAN_URL=https://hc-ping.com/your-uuid-here
